Subject: [PATCH] Bring the build status block up to date with the patches
 above it

Section 8 still read 4,171 passed at 91.39%. That was true when the
coverage commit wrote it and stopped being true four commits later: the
capacity stops, the store locking, the rate-confirmation distance and the
doctrine pin each brought their own tests and none of them touched the
status block.

Measured on this checkout rather than incremented:

  4,221 passed in 641.41s
  Required test coverage of 90.0% reached. Total coverage: 91.48%

A status block that drifts is worse than no status block, because a
cold-start builder has no way to know it drifted. It is the first table
in the file section 7 calls the source of truth.

